(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #161: a width of zero composes with a precision, so
 `{n:0.2}`, `{n:00.2}` and `{n:0.0}` print the places and pad nothing.)

a number called n is 63.
a float called ratio is 2.5.
Print "{n:0.2}".
Print "{n:00.2}".
Print "{n:0.0}".
Print "{ratio:0.2}".
Print "{ratio:00.3}".
a text called owed is "owed {n:0.2}".
Print owed.
a buffer called note is "note {ratio:0.1}".
Print note.

To 'show the amount' with a number called amount.
    Print "{amount:0.2}".

'show the amount' with 7.
